{
  "title": "Neutrophil\u2013eosinophil coupling does not robustly improve CRP prediction across NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "In 4,122 source and 4,927 target NHANES adults, adding neutrophil\u2013eosinophil coupling to nonlinear standard-measure models increased target log-CRP MSE by 0.000233 (0.022%). The source-refit/target-PSU 95% interval [-0.000957, 0.003682] spans benefit and harm; no robust incremental predictive utility was established.",
